import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Copyright & Sharing Policy | Murtaza Insights" description="How to share, quote and request permission to reuse Murtaza Insights articles, memes, cartoons and illustrations.">
  <section class="page-head wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Murtaza Insights</p>
    <h1>Copyright &amp; Sharing Policy</h1>
    <p>Please share the work with credit and a link to its original page.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap content-page">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>© 2026 <em>Murtaza Insights</em>. All rights reserved in the original material published here, subject to applicable law and any third-party rights noted on the site.</p>

      <h2>Sharing links and short extracts</h2>
      <p>You are welcome to share links to pages on <em>Murtaza Insights</em>, including through the website’s share buttons. You may quote a short extract from an article if you clearly credit <em>Murtaza Insights</em>, link to the original page and keep the quotation in context.</p>

      <h2>Sharing memes, cartoons and illustrations</h2>
      <p>You may share an original <em>Murtaza Insights</em> image on social media, WhatsApp or similar non-commercial channels. Keep the image intact, including its branding or signature, and include a link to its original page where possible. This permission does not extend to separately credited third-party images or material in which someone else holds rights.</p>

      <h2>When to request permission</h2>
      <p>Please ask before republishing a complete article or a substantial part of one; editing an image; removing a signature or branding; or using the content in advertising, products or other commercial material. Do not present the work as your own. Advertorials and other material involving third parties may require their permission as well.</p>
      <p>To request permission, use the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>. Please identify the article or image, where you would like to use it and whether the use is commercial.</p>

      <h2>Legal rights and credits</h2>
      <p>Nothing on this page limits uses permitted by applicable copyright law. Names, logos, photographs and other third-party material remain subject to their respective owners’ rights. Where a realistic or recognisable person appears in an AI-assisted illustration, an appropriate disclosure may be provided with the image or its caption; that disclosure is separate from these sharing terms.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
